  RELEVANCE: As one of the two foundational critical-exchange anthologies on Habermas's legal-political theory (alongside von Schomberg and Baynes 2002), this volume defines the terms of the Anglophone reception debate that subsequent secondary literature in this domain (Baxter, Zurn, Cronin) continues to engage.

  POSITION: Edited critical-exchange anthology; contributors span pluralist, systems-theoretic, and discourse-theoretic positions rather than a single school.
  },
  keywords = {discourse-theory-of-law, critical-exchanges, edited-volume, High, INCOMPLETE, no-abstract}
}

